  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "An invite, from its link to the keys it hands over: docs/API.md (Invites). A device in the home makes a random 32-byte token and shares it in a link; the joining device proves it holds the link, both show one six-digit code, and the approving device wraps the home's keys for it.",
    "The server gets only SHA-256 of the token's text, and the token sealed for the household. From the token come the proof, the code and the approval's MAC, each HMAC under HKDF(token, its name).",
    "Bytes are base64url without padding unless a field says hex or base64; strings are UTF-8; \"|\" joins the parts of a message, with nothing around it.",
    "HKDF is HKDF-SHA256 with salt \"petcam\" and 32 bytes out; HMAC is HMAC-SHA256; AES-GCM is AES-256-GCM with a 12-byte nonce and a 16-byte tag.",
    "Made by server/scripts/vectors.mjs from fixed keys that were made up for these files; nothing here was ever a real home's. No vector is ever removed: a format the apps stop opening stays, as one that must fail. Requests A and B are the ones SharedTests/InviteKeyBindingTests.swift has pinned since 2026-11-10. Read by SharedTests/InviteVectorTests.swift and server/test/vectors.test.ts."
  ],
